> Is there a way to get these casewise residuals as a range of 'plausible values', as is possible for the factor scores, as in Terrence's answer above?

You could do what Yves described.  After saving plausible values, and merging to your original data (see help-page examples), you can use the loadings to calculate predicted values of the observed variables, then calculate residuals.  Doing this within each data set returned by plausibleValues() would give you casewise distributions of residuals.

> plausibleValues() has type fixed at "lv"

Because plausible values are about factor scores.

